{
  "id": "recovery-probe-live-8",
  "title": "Recovery-loop live fixture v8 (rust + cargo validation)",
  "presentation": "primary",
  "origin": {
    "kind": "user"
  },
  "description": "Implement a small, well-tested addition to the Rust crate in this repository.\n\n## Task\nAdd a public function `pub fn classify_semantic(code: &str, message: &str) -> &'static str`\nto `src/lib.rs`, implementing exactly this recoverability split:\n\n- if `code` contains any of `gate-weaken`, `tamper`, `required-check` -> return `\"gate-weakening\"`\n- else if `code` contains any of `scope-ambigu`, `ambiguity` -> return `\"scope-ambiguity\"`\n- else if `code` contains any of `missing-authority`, `unauthorized`, `forged` -> return `\"missing-authority\"`\n- else if `code` contains any of `defect`, `incomplete-implementation`, `not-implemented` -> return `\"defect-or-incomplete-implementation\"`\n- else -> return `\"recoverable\"`\n\n`message` is accepted for signature stability but does not affect the result.\nAdd focused `#[cfg(test)]` unit tests covering at least one case per branch.\n\n## Validation\n- [ ] `cargo test --lib` is green\n- [ ] `cargo fmt --check` is clean\n- [ ] `cargo clippy` is clean\n- [ ] the function is public and the five branches are all covered by tests",
  "status": "in-progress",
